  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe upper level pattern features a strong ridge over the western\nCONUS as it transitions to a broad trough over the east. The\nmain jet remains to the north, helped by the presence of a mid\nlevel ridge over the southeastern CONUS. This is keeping the\nUpper OH Valley dry for a period of time.\n\nThe ensembles seem to be under playing the lower temperatures\nand have been a couple degree too warm. Have adjusted this down\na couple degrees. With the cooler dry conditions and clearing\nskies today, expect some frost to develop in the northeastern\ncounties as well as the eastern higher terrain. Thus, a Frost\nAdvisory has been issued for these areas for Tuesday morning.\nThe NBM probs are giving well over 70% probability for the\ndevelopment of frost.  \n\nConfidence remains high that dry conditions will persist through\nat least Saturday. The next potential for rainfall may come from\nthe remnants of a tropical disturbance currently being\nmonitored by the National Hurricane Center Sunday into Monday.",
